.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 429 AM PDT Sun Aug 2 2026

VFR everywhere except the coast where patchy stratus is filling in
over the Monterey Bay and San Mateo coastline. Given the
compressed marine layer, highest confidence in patchy IFR to LIFR
CIGs along the coast with stratus not expected to extend inland.
High pressure will keep the marine layer compressed again tonight
and see a late return of stratus along the coast. Currently not
expecting stratus to extend inland tonight due to the compressed
marine layer. Breezy onshore winds return this afternoon before
winds decrease overnight.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. The marine layer remains compressed due to
high pressure which will prevent stratus from extending inland.
Guidance shows some potential for patchy stratus to reach SFO
early this morning (12-16Z) but confidence is low that this will
occur. Breezy northwesterly winds expected this afternoon/evening
before winds decrease overnight.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...IFR to LIFR conditions expected this
morning. Some potential for patchy fog to impact MRY this morning
with visibilities decreasing to around 1-2SM. Conditions improve
by late morning with VFR through the afternoon. There is mixed
confidence on tonight`s stratus return. Ensemble guidance again
suggests a later return is likely at both sites with the HRRR
suggesting both sites could stay VFR through much of tonight. This
scenario cannot be fully written off due to how compressed the
marine layer is and the potential for high pressure to fully mix
out the marine layer. For the 06Z TAFs, leaned on persistence to
have stratus return late tonight but this may need to be amended
in future TAF issuances.

